ormulas, create or repair charts, clean or restructure tables, write concise summaries, or make explicit cell-range updates. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/acdd3141/skills/google-sheets/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-slides: Google Slides work for finding, reading, summarizing, creating, importing, visual cleanup, template migration, structural repair, and content edits in native Slides decks. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/acdd3141/skills/google-slides/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order: Generate a textbook-style stroke-order diagram (SVG) for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke showing completed strokes in black, the current stroke highlighted with a red number and directional arrow at its starting point, and remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill whenever the user asks how to write a Japanese character, requests stroke order, asks \"in what order do I draw X\", wants to learn or memorize a kanji, asks to decompose a character into strokes, says \"show me the strokes for X\", mentions 書き順 / kakijun, or shows a stroke-order chart and asks for one for a different character. Trigger even when the user only provides a single character and the intent is implicit from the language-learning context. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/kanji-stroke-order/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-knowledge-capture: Capture conversations and decisions into structured Notion pages; use when turning chats/notes into wiki entries, how-tos, decisions, or FAQs with proper linking. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/notion/acdd3141/skills/notion-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-meeting-intelligence: Prepare meeting materials with Notion context and Codex research; use when gathering context, drafting agendas/pre-reads, and tailoring materials to attendees. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/notion/ac